WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.924
Responsible communication protects accuracy and reduces harm.

00:00:03.924 --> 00:00:05.540
Avoid overclaiming.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:11.772
State the claim examined, evidence reviewed, conclusion reached, confidence, and important limitations.

00:00:11.772 --> 00:00:16.620
Separate technical observations from judgments about authenticity or intent.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.697
Use labels precisely.

00:00:18.697 --> 00:00:22.160
Unverified means available evidence is insufficient.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.084
Manipulated means supported alterations changed the media.

00:00:26.084 --> 00:00:30.008
Synthetic means generation is supported by evidence.

00:00:30.008 --> 00:00:37.625
Miscontextualized means genuine or partly genuine media is paired with a false or misleading context.

00:00:37.625 --> 00:00:40.626
These labels are not interchangeable.

00:00:40.626 --> 00:00:48.243
A clip can be unverified without being fake, and manipulated media can contain genuine events.

00:00:48.243 --> 00:00:54.476
Disinformation additionally implies deceptive intent, which may require evidence beyond the file.

00:00:54.476 --> 00:00:58.400
Use calibrated confidence language and explain why.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:06.017
High confidence should reflect strong provenance, independent corroboration, consistent technical findings, and limited plausible alternatives.

00:01:06.017 --> 00:01:10.403
A detector score alone does not justify certainty.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:17.097
Sensitive media may involve victims, private individuals, sexual content, violence, or reputational accusations.

00:01:17.097 --> 00:01:25.176
Limit distribution, avoid unnecessary reproduction, protect personal details, and follow legal, safeguarding, and organizational reporting procedures.

00:01:25.176 --> 00:01:28.177
Support truth without amplifying harm.

00:01:28.177 --> 00:01:36.718
Lead with verified context rather than sensational repetition, correct errors promptly, and preserve evidence for accountable review.

00:01:36.718 --> 00:01:44.335
The best report helps the audience make a proportionate decision while remaining honest about uncertainty.
